### D.4 Chunk-Causal Sliding-Window Attention

VideoMLA preserves the chunk-causal attention pattern used by the autoregressive Wan backbone. Tokens within the same 3-latent-frame chunk can attend to one another, while tokens in a later chunk cannot be attended to by earlier chunks. For long-horizon generation, attention is restricted to a fixed cache consisting of one sink latent frame and the most recent six latent frames. Since each latent frame contains 1560 tokens, the sink occupies 1560 cached token slots and the local window occupies 6×15606\times 1560 token slots.

